# End-to-end: a small domain where VERIFY must come before PROPOSE.
#
# Six test files; hidden concept S = "an integration test" (touches the network or a database).
# The initial vocabulary has only slow and doc, so two pairs share a class:
# {0,4} and {2,5}. Ask one representative per class and the status reads IDENTIFIED,
# but the labels of 4 and 5 were inherited from their class-mates -- need must ask for VERIFY.

objects 6
add slow 0 1 4
add doc 0 2 4 5

# One representative per class.
vote 0 3 0     # f0 is an integration test
vote 1 0 3     # f1 is not
vote 2 3 0     # f2 is
vote 3 0 3     # f3 is not
need           # expect IDENTIFIED / VERIFY / unverified=[4,5]

# Probe f4: it is not an integration test, so it collides with f0.
vote 4 0 3
need           # expect INSUFFICIENT / PROPOSE

# Propose a new atom: touches the network (f0 and f2).
add net 0 2
need           # expect UNDETERMINED / ASK (5 has not been asked directly)
vote 5 3 0     # f5 touches a database, so it is an integration test as well
need           # expect IDENTIFIED / STOP (every class is a singleton, no inherited label)

status
explain
